WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.294
Spherical CNNs generalize convolutional networks to
signals living on the sphere,

00:00:05.374 --> 00:00:09.408
which makes them a natural fit for molecules and
weather data.

00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:13.920
But until now they were stuck at low resolutions
and shallow depths,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.834
so they never really competed on large real-world
problems.

00:00:17.914 --> 00:00:22.080
This paper, Scaling Spherical CNNs from Google
Research and MIT,

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.128
shows how to scale these models by a full order of
magnitude.

00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:29.644
With new activations, normalization, residual blocks,

00:00:29.724 --> 00:00:31.966
and a TPU-optimized implementation,

00:00:32.046 --> 00:00:37.805
the authors reach state of the art on the QM9
molecular benchmark and become competitive

00:00:37.885 --> 00:00:40.260
on several weather forecasting tasks.
